 « VFX Artist UE5 » recoupe mon travail quotidien : Houdini, Unreal Engine, Niagara et Substance.\n\nCe que je recherche aujourd’hui, c’est un contrat, avec une équipe engagée sur un projet ambitieux. J’ai besoin de travailler avec des professionnels expérimentés et de m’inscrire dans une dynamique collective, quelque chose que le travail en solo, aussi formateur soit-il, ne permet pas de retrouver.\n\nJe serais heureux de pouvoir échanger avec vous par téléphone ou en visioconférence, selon votre disponibilité.\n\nMatthieu Huguet\n===== Ripple & Roll | Technical Artist : Stylised Rendering (Environments) | offer 89 en offer\nFreelance proposal for Technical Artist : Stylised Rendering (Environments): Matthieu Huguet, Technical Artist\nTo the recruitment team,\n\nHello Ripple & Roll,\n\nI am writing about your need for Technical Artist : Stylised Rendering (Environments), which I can take on as a freelancer.\n\nMy name is Matthieu Huguet, I am 25 and I work as a freelance Technical Artist, based in Aix-en-Provence, France.\n\nI studied a Game Design Bachelor at LISAA Paris, a Master’s at ARTFX Montpellier, then technical art courses at Gnomon and through Harvard CS50, before going freelance in early 2025.\n\nI worked on an NDA project with Meerkat Studio and on an archviz project for a private client in Aix-en-Provence. All my work can be seen at matthieuhuguet.com.\n\nRight now I am working on integrating and building solutions with Cursor and Claude, connected to Houdini and Unreal, that generate level design through HDAs and let me iterate on it quickly. My latest published work: Ceramic Tiles, HDA Stairs Component and UV Texture Variation Offset.\n\nYour opening for Technical Artist : Stylised Rendering (Environments) lines up with my day-to-day work: Houdini.\n\nWhat I am looking for today is a contract with a team committed to an ambitious project. I need to work with experienced professionals and be part of a collective dynamic, something that working solo, h