astmod>${lastmod}</lastmod>` : ''}</url>`).join('')}</urlset>`\n\ndescribe('helpers', () => {\n  it('reads sitemaps and indexes, and turns slugs into words without ids', () => {\n    expect(parseSitemap(sitemap(['https://a.com/jobs/x', '2026-10-01'], ['https://a.com/jobs/y']))).toEqual([{ loc: 'https://a.com/jobs/x', lastmod: '2026-10-01' }, { loc: 'https://a.com/jobs/y', lastmod: '' }])\n    expect(slugWords('https://a.com/jobs/keywords-studios-3d-dfac1c36.html')).toBe('jobs keywords studios 3d')\n    expect(slugWords('https://www.gamesjobsdirect.com/job/counterpunch/2d-pixel-artist/361465')).toBe('job counterpunch 2d pixel artist')\n  })\n  it('tolerates the three defects found in real JSON-LD, and still refuses garbage', () => {\n    expect(tolerantJson('{\"a\":\"x\\\\_y\"}')).toEqual({ a: 'x_y' })\n    expect(tolerantJson('{\"a\":\"x\\ny\"}')).toEqual({ a: 'x y' })\n    expect(tolerantJson('{\"a\":{\"b\":\"c\";}, \"d\":1;\"e\":2}')).toEqual({ a: { b: 'c' }, d: 1, e: 2 })\n    expect(tolerantJson('{bad')).toBeNull()\n    expect(jobPosting('<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@type\":\"JobPosting\",\"title\":\"T\";}</script>').title).toBe('T')\n  })\n  it('a posting becomes a listing; expired, nameless or off-topic ones do not', () => {\n    const make = (p) => listingFromPosting(p, { url: 'https://a.com/j/1', site: 's', label: 'S', today: '2026-10-07' })\n    expect(make(posting('Technical Artist'))).toMatchObject({ lane: 'games', name: 'Acme Games', country: 'FR', location: 'Lyon', sourceKey: 'index:s' })\n    expect(make(posting('Technical Artist', 'Acme', { validThrough: '2026-10-06' }))).toBeNull()\n    expect(make({ ...posting('Technical Artist'), hiringOrganization: '' })).toBeNull()\n    expect(make(posting('Chief Marketing Officer'))).toBeNull()\n    expect(make(posting('Technical Artist', 'Acme', { jobLocation: { address: { addressLocality: 'null', addressCountry: 'null' } } }))).toMatchObject({ location: '', country: '' })\n  })\n})\n\ndescribe('sitemap strategy', () => {\n  const site = { enabled: true, label: 'S', strategy: 'sitemap', sitemaps: ['https://a.com/sitemap.xml'], jobPath: '/jobs/', recencyDays: 30, maxDetails: 2 }\n  const pages = {\n    'https://a.com/sitemap.xml': sitemap(['https://a.com/jobs/acme-technical-artist-aaaa1111.html', '2026-10-06'], ['https://a.com/jobs/acme-vfx-artist-bbbb2222.html', '2026-10-05'], ['https://a.com/jobs/acme-houdini-artist-cccc3333.html', '2026-10-04'], ['https://a.com/jobs/acme-accountant-dddd4444.html', '2026-10-06'], ['https://a.com/jobs/old-environment-artist-eeee5555.html', '2025-01-01']),\n    'https://a.com/jobs/acme-technical-artist-aaaa1111.html': ld(posting('Technical Artist')),\n    'https://a.com/jobs/acme-vfx-artist-bbbb2222.html': ld(posting('Sales Intern')),\n    'https://a.com/jobs/acme-houdini-artist-cccc3333.html': ld(posting('Houdini Artist')),\n  }\n  it('prefilters by slug and recency, respects the cap, newest first, and remembers what it judged irrelevant', async () => {\n    const fetcher = fakeFetcher(pages); const seen = createSeenCache()\n    const [board] = await indexes({ http: {}, config: cfg({ s: site }), fetcher, seen, now: NOW })\n    expect(board.key).toBe('index:s'); expect(board.listed).toBe(5)\n    expect(board.listings.map((l) => l.title)).toEqual(['Technical Artist'])\n    expect(fetcher.calls.filter((c) => c.includes('/jobs/'))).toEqual(['https://a.com/jobs/acme-technical-artist-aaaa1111.html', 'https://a.com/jobs/acme-vfx-artist-bbbb2222.html'])\n    expect(await seen.has('https://a.com/jobs/acme-vfx-artist-bbbb2222.html')).toBe(true)\n    // second pass: the kept page is known by the store, the irrelevant one is remembered, so the cap reaches the next page\n    const again = fakeFetcher(pages)\n    const [second] = await indexes({ http: {}, config: cfg({ s: site }), fetcher: again, seen, known: new Set(['https://a.com/jobs/acme-technical-artist-aaaa1111.html']), now: NOW })\n    expect(again.calls.filter((c) => c.includes('/jobs/'))).toEqual(['https://a.com/jobs/acme-houdini-artist-cccc3333.html'])\n    expect(second.listings.map((l) => l.title)).toEqual(['Houdini Artist'])\n  })\n  it('never closes anything: the board is a window, not a catalogue', async () => {\n    const [board] = await indexes({ http: {}, config: cfg({ s: site }), fetcher: fakeFetcher(pages), seen: createSeenCache(), now: NOW })\n    expect(board.complete).toBe(false); expect(board.partial).toBe(true)\n  })\n  it('ids are stable across passes and a nested sitemap index is followed', async () => {\n    const nested = { 'https://a.com/sitemap.xml': '<sitemapindex><sitemap><loc>https://a.com/sitemap-jobs.xml</loc></sitemap></sitemapindex>', 'https://a.com/sitemap-jobs.xml': pages['https://a.com/sitemap.xml'], ...pages }\n    const one = await indexes({ http: {}, config: cfg({ s: site }), fetcher: fakeFetcher(nested), seen: createSeenCache(), now: NOW })\n    const two = await indexes({ http: {}, config: cfg({ s: site }), fetcher: fakeFetcher(nested), seen: createSeenCache(), now: NOW })\n    expect(one[0].seenIds).toEqual(two[0].seenIds); expect(one[0].seenIds).toHaveLength(1)\n  })\n})\n\ndescribe('other strategies', () => {\n  it('devquest: one data file, only recent matching jobs, direct links', async () => {\n    const data = { jobs: [\n      { id: 'a', title: 'Technical Artist', studio: 'Riot Games', url: 'https://jobs.lever.co/x/1', firstSeen: '2026-10-05T00:00:00Z', location: 'Paris', workType: 'Full-time', tech: ['Houdini'] },\n      { id: 'b', title: 'Accountant', studio: 'Riot Games', url: 'https://jobs.lever.co/x/2', firstSeen: '2026-10-05T00:00:00Z' },\n      { id: 'c', title: 'VFX Artist', studio: 'Old Studio', url: 'https://jobs.lever.co/x/3', firstSeen: '2025-01-01T00:00:00Z' },\n      { id: 'd', title: 'Level Artist', studio: 'No Link', url: '', firstSeen: '2026-10-05T00:00:00Z' },\n    ] }\n    const fetcher = fakeFetcher({ 'https://devquest.gg/jobs.js': `window.JOBS_DATA = ${JSON.stringify(data)};` })